# Use Tailwind for New UI

This app is styled with Tailwind CSS 4 (`@import "tailwindcss"` in `src/index.css`, Vite plugin in `vite.config.ts`). Style every new component, page, and feature with Tailwind utility classes on `className`.

## Do

- Use Tailwind utilities for layout, spacing, typography, color, borders, and hover/focus states
- Match existing tokens: `slate` for neutrals, `indigo` for accents, `emerald` / `rose` for positive / negative
- Use `className` template strings (or `clsx` / `cn`) for conditional classes
- Prefer composing utilities over adding CSS

## Don't

- Don't add CSS modules, Sass, styled-components, Emotion, or other CSS-in-JS
- Don't add new `.css` files or extra component rules in `src/index.css`
- Don't use inline `style={{}}` except for values Tailwind cannot express (for example a dynamic width from data)

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — inline styles or custom CSS
<div style={{ padding: 20, background: "white" }} />

// ✅ GOOD — Tailwind utilities matching existing cards
<div className="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
  <h1 className="pb-6 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Budgets</h1>
  <p className={`text-sm font-semibold ${over ? "text-rose-500" : "text-emerald-600"}`}>
    {label}
  </p>
</div>
```
